  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are nnn friends. The ithi^{\\text{th}}ith friend has AiA_iAi​ coins. You are also given an integer RRR.\n\nDefine a transaction as the transfer of one coin from one friend to another. They can do as many transactions as they want under the constraint that:\n\n\nFor any ordered pair of friends iii and jjj, the number of transactions from iii to jjj doesn't exceed RRR.\nWhat is the maximum possible number of coins the friend with the minimum coins can have in the end?\n\nPlease note that the number of coins held by a person can't go negative at any time in the process of transactions.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain nnn and RRR.\nThen the second line contains nnn integers separated by a space, A1,A2,…,AnA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_nA1​,A2​,…,An​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint the maximum possible number of coins the friend with the minimum coins can have in the end.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤n≤1051 \\leq n \\leq 10^51≤n≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤R≤1031 \\leq R \\leq 10^31≤R≤103"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
